{"posts":[{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_101","t":"Q: how many candle needed to make it a base?\n\nA: Don't get too hung up on the candle count. Focus more on how the price moved away from the level. You want to see a violent burst of liquidity (pole) coming out of the level.","a":"ppvp","d":"","n":"#101","p":5,"im":[],"m":101},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_102","t":"Tyoon wrote: I think what you were marking were not bases but reactions.\n\nGiven what you said above I have this question now:\n\nAre these bases not to be considered as such but as reactions to previous zone? If not, how do I catalogue them? How can I use them?","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#102","p":5,"im":["716bd9d76f2c4824437d9464957b7f8d9f0e83de"],"m":102},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_103","t":"04 of 20","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#103","p":5,"im":["a7feeede64deba0ef4b085fd5d3e95054595f867"],"m":103},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_104","t":"Every DBR and RBD has its own importance and value, and nearly every one can be traded. For each one that you find, zoom out to the HTFs, and see what historical significance the decision point has. Perhaps it's a failure to get back into an important PA Zone - these ones are special. Perhaps it's within an HTF compression zone to the left - ask yourself would you take this trade, or wait for the tip of the zone?\n\nThe bigger picture will always help you decide on the significance of a DBR/RBD","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#104","p":5,"im":[],"m":104},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_105","t":"hornet wrote: Are these bases not to be considered as such but as reactions to previous zone? If not, how do I catalogue them? How can I use them?\n\nSorry I did not reply earlier. Yes what you have shown there is stacked demand. The base is easily seen on the 4h. The base was created in reaction to a support level IMO.","a":"Tyoon","d":"","n":"#105","p":5,"im":["af08266df4f206452359af639b44f3009c9ccce9"],"m":105},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_106","t":"Question - A Valid RBD","a":"justinforex","d":"","n":"#106","p":5,"im":["a541caf0a2b981e628869ce82066336847ebeb69"],"m":106},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_107","t":"justinforex wrote: Question - A Valid RBD\n\nIt does not have to break the previous H/L to become a valid base.\n\nWhat defines a base it that price moves up or down, bases (consolidates, congests, clusters, ect) then moves again either up or down.\n\nHere are the variations. The standard DBD and RBR then the RBR and DBD then RBD during downtrend and DBR during uptrend.\n\nHopefully this could give you a better understanding. However as you have alluded to, H/L or S/R levels are almost always an intrinsic part to the development of any base. If you can find the levels responsible for the bases it can give you a much holistic picture on the chart.","a":"Tyoon","d":"","n":"#107","p":5,"im":["539fc9d9e3af2f1c1b357a1b033f2f02ec863c12"],"m":107},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_108","t":"The two charts on the right, in HTF, can often look just like the two charts on the left. It's worth looking into these on your charts, and finding out which tend to perform better on price return - drop/consolidation/drops or drop/RBD/Drops, and the same for rallies","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#108","p":5,"im":[],"m":108},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_109","t":"Hi guys,\n\nThese are my attempt on identifying these patterns. I know there's a lot more of these patterns that I didnt mark on the chart, I'm just taking the obvious one.\n\nAll feedback are welcomed, thank you.","a":"Neopips","d":"","n":"#109","p":5,"im":["e1fda8394b7248d3c4a6facf97b8032c3610e112","03b6e385ab6bae868abb33e08da08dddcebbe283"],"m":109},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_110","t":"wow, you are blessed whit the \"IF candles\"\n\nAnyway, good job. But when a zone looks messy, go down into LTF and draw some line, you can be surprised. in the chart the LTF of the first 2 on your chart [the spike probably is a news spike]","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#110","p":5,"im":["e0bed6d1178c191df7cad87e5cf099e3531ea1d5"],"m":110},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_111","t":"Hi Guys,\n\nRBD & DBR for review. Appreciating your help. Thank you in advance.\n\nR.","a":"Rogeid16","d":"","n":"#111","p":5,"im":["4824cfcfa6351b039e8f1a71287cba90e5ebfd0e"],"m":111},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_112","t":"i think i hav better understanding now. thans for the explaination.\n\nwil try do more practice to improve.","a":"justinforex","d":"","n":"#112","p":5,"im":[],"m":112},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_113","t":"05 of 20","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#113","p":5,"im":["e3066b1bbcb90952124c2bdddd347f80fb22dbbf"],"m":113},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_114","t":"Hi Hornet,\n\nI notted different things on your 4th Chart. Let me know if you need more explaination. Best, Mel","a":"@mel","d":"","n":"#114","p":5,"im":["fd7c68a688d2fd035fa59d7d3648612ce882ed94"],"m":114},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_115","t":"06 OF 20","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#115","p":5,"im":["6830efc971c2ec8a37c17836c010c04b16b23bd9"],"m":115},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_116","t":"AUDUSD M15\n\nUSDCAD m15","a":"Neopips","d":"","n":"#116","p":5,"im":["4b06f45f9ba84355b5c95d6bdb53134cfbb2bfb4","4fc08bb19296322bcba93f6026da947a40a62a61"],"m":116},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_117","t":"EURUSD m30:","a":"Neopips","d":"","n":"#117","p":5,"im":["5c2cf547fe69e882627de0417c12a6733e62bd53"],"m":117},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_118","t":"~^o^~","a":"MitchWorse","d":"","n":"#118","p":5,"im":[],"m":118},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_119","t":"07 of 20","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#119","p":5,"im":["db179778274fdb813a144f203549f2bf8927aeb9"],"m":119},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_120","t":"@mel wrote: Hi Hornet,\n\nI notted different things on your 4th Chart. Let me know if you need more explaination. Best, Mel\n\nHi Mel,\n\nall is well. I understand your points and agree with them. Thanks for taking the time.\n\nMichael","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#120","p":5,"im":[],"m":120},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_121","t":"Neopips wrote: EURUSD m30:\n\nthat is a great chart!!!","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#121","p":5,"im":["5c2cf547fe69e882627de0417c12a6733e62bd53"],"m":121},{"id":"dbrrbd_p5_122","t":"Sorry just seeing this I will consult my notes and advise getting ready for school right now","a":"Nosbigs","d":"","n